{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create the appworker account on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The account was created with UID/GID 1001, home /home/appworker, and shell /bin/bash. Its account and home remained present after the node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f02160b7038f4610","cmd-a57a957a877e4f1c","cmd-81e7a1f616164667"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Apply limits of 8,192 open files and 256 processes to appworker login sessions.","status":"satisfied","summary":"PAM-backed appworker login sessions directly reported matching soft and hard limits for both resources before and after restart; /proc/self/limits corroborated the effective values.","evidence_ids":["cmd-560ff36047c549ea","cmd-a57a957a877e4f1c","cmd-f7a45907aa9f4d17","cmd-81e7a1f616164667"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use a legacy-platform-compatible solution.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL Server 7.9 and kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 were unchanged after execution and restart. The implementation used native account, PAM limits, and system utilities already available on the platform, with no package or platform replacement.","evidence_ids":["cmd-560ff36047c549ea","cmd-f02160b7038f4610","cmd-81e7a1f616164667","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All substantive mutations were causally related to creating the account, configuring its limits, or executing the mandatory restart protocol. The initial unprivileged useradd attempt stopped before changing state. One minor hygiene concern is the reboot launcher’s creation of /var/tmp/antrieb-reboot.log: it was not subsequently read or cleaned, and the lifecycle inventory did not cover /var/tmp, so its final presence is unverified. No failed services, unexpected listening sockets, or security weakening were observed after execution.","evidence_ids":["cmd-49cba684f2f247e4","cmd-b0ecd72d392847a7","cmd-f02160b7038f4610","cmd-cf04ddbc22fd4f99","cmd-81e7a1f616164667","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct effective-session testing and post-restart persistence evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, an outage was observed, the boot ID changed, and the system, account, limits, services, and normal sockets recovered. Fixed lifecycle observations independently corroborate the boot transition and unchanged platform.","limitations":["Native package-health checks timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency could not be independently assessed.","The lifecycle temporary-file inventory covered /tmp but not /var/tmp, so the final disposition of /var/tmp/antrieb-reboot.log is not directly observed."]}
